From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 23:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] (hybris) Don't switch root to /first_stage_ramdisk

Bootloaders of recovery-as-boot devices pass
androidboot.force_normal_boot=1, which makes first stage init
SwitchRoot() to /first_stage_ramdisk. Under hybris the root
filesystem is set up by Mer/systemd, so moving its mounts fails
("Unable to move mount at '/data': Invalid argument") and
droid-hal-init exits with status 6.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 init/first_stage_init.cpp | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/init/first_stage_init.cpp b/init/first_stage_init.cpp
--- a/init/first_stage_init.cpp
+++ b/init/first_stage_init.cpp
@@ -276,7 +276,9 @@ int FirstStageMain(int argc, char** argv) {
         StartConsole();
     }
 
-    if (ForceNormalBoot(cmdline)) {
+    // hybris: the root filesystem is set up by Mer/systemd; switching to
+    // /first_stage_ramdisk would try to move its mounts (e.g. /data) and fail.
+    if (/*ForceNormalBoot(cmdline)*/ false) {
         mkdir("/first_stage_ramdisk", 0755);
         // SwitchRoot() must be called with a mount point as the target, so we bind mount the
         // target directory to itself here.
-- 
